{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791688590,"nonce":"sly04b7Xy18PC5V7B2wSThnIn2I=","message":"Decision: db restore does not run systemctl itself. It refuses (exit 1, printing the systemctl stop commands for container and host units) when /proc shows another process with the db, -wal or -shm open or a running jobhunter console process (cmdline scan, since the console opens a connection per request); --force overrides with a warning. It takes the C5 lock non-blocking and refuses if held. Reason: stopping user services is a side effect the user should choose; the run lock already keeps timer jobs out during the restore.","files":null}]}